Usages:
  merge_semantics: |
    Table never interprets item contents. On every background merge of parts, it invokes the
    caller-supplied PrepareBlockCallback with the raw sorted byte-string items about to be
    written, letting the caller transform, deduplicate, or drop items before they hit disk.
    This is the only domain-specific hook in the whole engine — everything else operates on
    opaque, lexicographically-sortable byte slices.

Annotations: |
  This cell is a generic, storage-domain-agnostic merge-sorted key-value engine — a lightweight
  LSM-tree: items are buffered in-memory, converted into immutable compressed parts, and
  background-merged using a size-tiered strategy, with sorted iteration/prefix-seek search over
  the merged view. It has no knowledge of tags, metric IDs, or time series.

  Use `merge_semantics` to understand how a caller (e.g. an inverted index) layers
  domain-specific merge behavior on top without this cell's involvement.

---

"Table(path: string, flushInterval: time.Duration, prepareBlock: PrepareBlockCallback, isReadOnly: bool)":
  location: table.go
  annotations: |
    Obtained via the MustOpenTable factory. Owns the full lifecycle of ingested items: an
    in-memory buffer, background conversion to compressed on-disk/in-memory parts, background
    merging of parts, and snapshotting.

    `path`: on-disk directory for this table's parts
    `flushInterval`: how often buffered in-memory data is force-flushed
    `prepareBlock`: see `merge_semantics`
    `isReadOnly`: when true, disables background merging (e.g. during a read-only replica mode)
  methods:
    "AddItems(items: [][]byte)": |
      Ingest new sorted-key items into the table's in-memory buffer.
    "UpdateMetrics(m: TableMetrics)": |
      Populate `m` with the table's current size/throughput counters.
    "DebugFlush()": |
      Force all buffered in-memory data to become searchable immediately (used by tests and
      admin endpoints, not the hot path).
    "MustCreateSnapshotAt(dstDir: string)": |
      Hard-link all current parts into `dstDir`, producing a consistent point-in-time snapshot.
    "Path() -> path:string": |
      Return the table's on-disk directory.
    "MustClose()": |
      Stop all background merge/flush goroutines and release resources.

"TableMetrics()":
  location: table.go
  annotations: |
    Plain snapshot of table-level counters (items added, in-memory/file part counts, data-block
    cache size, etc.), populated in place by `Table`'s own UpdateMetrics method.
  methods:
    "TotalItemsCount() -> count:uint64": |
      Sum of items currently held across in-memory and on-disk parts.

"Item(start: uint32, end: uint32)":
  location: encoding.go
  annotations: |
    A lightweight offset-pair view into a shared byte buffer — the unit `Table` and
    `PrepareBlockCallback` operate on. Avoids per-item allocation: many `Item`s reference slices
    of one larger buffer.
  methods:
    "Bytes(data: []byte) -> value:[]byte": |
      Resolve this item's byte range against the shared buffer `data`.
    "String(data: []byte) -> value:string": |
      Same as this type's own Bytes method, returned as a string.

"PrepareBlockCallback(data: []byte, items: []Item) -> data:[]byte, items:[]Item":
  location: merge.go
  annotations: |
    Caller-supplied hook invoked during every background merge of parts, before the merged
    block is written out.

    `data`: shared backing buffer for `items`
    `items`: sorted `Item`s about to be merged into one block

    Use `merge_semantics` for what implementations of this callback are expected to do.

    Requirements:
    - Returned `items` must remain sorted and reference valid ranges of the returned `data`

"TableSearch(tb: Table, sparse: bool)":
  location: table_search.go
  annotations: |
    Reusable cursor for sorted iteration and prefix-seek search over a `Table`.

    `sparse`: when true, uses a lighter-weight index-block cache suited for infrequent,
    full-table scans instead of hot repeated lookups.
  properties:
    "Item -> []byte": |
      The item at the cursor's current position; valid only right after a successful call to
      this type's own NextItem or FirstItemWithPrefix method.
  methods:
    "Seek(k: []byte)": |
      Position the cursor at the first item greater than or equal to `k`.
    "FirstItemWithPrefix(prefix: []byte) -> err:error": |
      Position the cursor at the first item starting with `prefix`.
    "NextItem() -> found:bool": |
      Advance the cursor; `found` is false once no more items are available.
    "Error() -> err:error": |
      Return any error encountered during iteration.
    "MustClose()": |
      Release resources held by this cursor.

"SetIndexBlocksCacheSize(size: int)":
  location: part.go
  annotations: |
    Set the process-wide cache size (in bytes) for decoded index blocks shared across all
    tables in the process.

"SetDataBlocksCacheSize(size: int)":
  location: part.go
  annotations: |
    Set the process-wide cache size (in bytes) for decoded data blocks used by hot,
    repeated (non-sparse) searches.

"SetDataBlocksSparseCacheSize(size: int)":
  location: part.go
  annotations: |
    Set the process-wide cache size (in bytes) for decoded data blocks used by sparse,
    infrequent (e.g. full-scan) searches; see `TableSearch`'s sparse parameter.

